I only needed to use up one tripe ration (well, that was all I had...).

Here's what I did: (major "cleaning-out-shops" spoiler)

First make sure that the area in front of the entrance has an item
in every square, so the dog will be encouraged to drop things right
in the empty square that you are going to stand behind.  That square
is not part of the store, and you don't have to pay for anything
you pick up from that square.

Then stand in the doorway and wait for the dog to drop something in
front of you...

 (1)       (2)       (3)       (4)       (5)       (6)      (7)

 ####      ####      ####      ####      ####      ####     ####     
 ![)#      ![)#      ![)#      ![)#      ![)#      ![)#     ![)#     
 %@@+##    %@ @##    %@d@##    %@!@##    %@!@##    %@@+##   %@ @##   
 d//#      *d/#      *//#      */d#      *d/#      d//#     *//#     
 ####      ####      ####      ####      ####      ####     ####     
                                 ^
                                 |
                               Toss the tripe here

I think that the first tripe ration he gets is enough encouragement.
The first time I tried this we totally cleaned out the shop in very
short order.  A couple of times the dog sat in the corner without
moving.  All I had to do was step into the shop and move around a
little, then step back out, and the little dog would get back to work.

Maybe if I had more tripe rations I could get him even *better* trained.
But he seems to do quite well after one ration.

